Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: Phase A object models as they land; may begin after #183 with incremental coverage.

## Goal
Provide a reusable dependency/reference model so destructive schema changes, Explorer navigation and migration planning share the same object relationship graph.

## Scope
Relationships such as:
- table -> indexes/constraints/triggers/views;
- column -> constraints/indexes/views/routines where provider exposes dependencies;
- view -> referenced tables/views;
- routine -> referenced objects where reliably introspectable;
- sequence -> owned-by / dependents;
- type/domain/enum -> dependent columns/routines;
- schema -> contained objects.

UI:
- Dependencies tab;
- Referenced By tab;
- navigate to object;
- copy qualified name;
- risk summary before destructive mutation.

Architecture:
- canonical dependency service/model;
- provider adapters collect metadata;
- mutation/migration layers consume the same graph rather than implementing their own dependency lookup.

## Acceptance
- deterministic object identities across schemas/connections;
- dependency direction clearly distinguished from reverse references;
- destructive preview can show meaningful dependent objects;
- missing/unsupported dependency metadata is explicit, never fabricated;
- large dependency sets are bounded/virtualized;
- PostgreSQL coverage plus appropriate SQLite subset;
- service/provider/native UI tests.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(schema): add object dependency navigator`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: Monitoring foundation #196 for richer live context; basic EXPLAIN may proceed from Query infrastructure.
Authority: `docs/goals/goal-phase-h-ai.md`

## Goal
Build a canonical query-plan analysis surface that humans can use directly and Agent tools can reuse later.

## Scope
- EXPLAIN result parsing/model;
- EXPLAIN ANALYZE only behind explicit warning because it executes the query;
- plan tree visualization;
- cost/rows/time/loops/buffers where provider exposes them;
- highlight expensive nodes, seq scans, misestimates and sort/hash hotspots using deterministic heuristics;
- link referenced tables/indexes to Explorer;
- copy/export plan;
- optional AI explanation only after canonical plan model exists.

## Safety
- EXPLAIN ANALYZE is LongRunning/possibly mutating depending SQL; classify through canonical statement/action safety before execution;
- never auto-run ANALYZE on destructive/mutation SQL;
- AI receives bounded plan/schema context, not unrestricted data.

## Acceptance
- representative PostgreSQL JSON plan parses deterministically;
- nested plans render and remain usable for large trees;
- user can distinguish estimate-only EXPLAIN from runtime ANALYZE;
- heuristic findings reference exact plan nodes;
- Agent explanation reuses same plan model/service, not a second EXPLAIN implementation;
- service/native UI/live PG tests.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(query): add query plan visualizer and advisor`

Parent Goal: #182

## Goal
Add a native diagnostics surface that makes crashes, provider failures, worker errors and environment problems inspectable without exposing secrets.

## Scope
Settings/Diagnostics or dedicated support panel:
- app version/build SHA;
- OS/arch;
- provider versions where known;
- recent structured application errors;
- log file location/open action;
- copy diagnostics summary;
- export support bundle;
- feature/capability snapshot;
- recent failed jobs/tasks where applicable.

## Support bundle
May include:
- sanitized logs;
- app/version metadata;
- capability matrix snapshot;
- non-secret settings summary;
- crash/error records.

Must exclude by default:
- DB passwords;
- AI provider keys;
- SSH secrets/private keys;
- full query/data contents unless user explicitly opts in.

## Acceptance
- secrets/connection URLs are redacted deterministically;
- support bundle content is previewable before save;
- log rotation/retention bounded;
- panic/provider/runtime errors have stable structured IDs where practical;
- export works on supported desktop platforms;
- tests cover redaction and bundle contents.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(diagnostics): add native diagnostics and support bundle`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #206

## Goal
Extend saved/manual tasks into an explicit scheduler without weakening confirmation, capability or credential boundaries.

## Scope
- cron-like schedule model;
- enable/disable schedule;
- next/last run;
- retry policy;
- execution history;
- failure notification surface inside app;
- per-task target connection/context;
- app-start catch-up policy explicitly defined;
- cancellation where supported.

## Safety
- destructive/admin task types must not become silently schedulable by default;
- credentials referenced by connection id/secret store only;
- production-environment tasks require stronger policy/confirmation when schedule is created or modified;
- app-not-running semantics must be explicit: no fake background scheduler unless a real service exists.

## Acceptance
- scheduled non-destructive task executes once at expected time while app scheduler is active;
- duplicate execution prevented across restart/recovery;
- missed-run behavior deterministic;
- disable/delete prevents future runs;
- run history distinguishes scheduled/manual/retry;
- destructive scheduling policy enforced centrally;
- persistence/service/native UI tests.

Merge independently after J01.
Suggested commit: `feat(tasks): add scheduled database task execution`

Parent Goal: #182
Authority: `docs/goals/goal-phase-g-productivity.md`

## Goal
Add a first-class Data Activity for fast return to frequently used tables/results without duplicating the Table Data Editor or Result Grid.

## Scope
Sidebar sections:
- Recent Tables;
- Pinned Tables;
- Recent Query Results where persistence semantics permit;
- recent exports as references only if useful.

Actions:
- open table data;
- open table structure;
- new query for table;
- export;
- copy qualified name;
- pin/unpin;
- remove from recent.

## Architecture
Reuse canonical Table workspace, Query Result grid and local workspace/meta persistence. Do not build a second data-grid state system.

## Acceptance
- recent table access updates deterministically;
- pinned tables survive restart and connection reconnect;
- missing/deleted objects degrade gracefully;
- multi-connection duplicate table names remain unambiguous;
- selecting item opens canonical workspace/tab;
- no result data is persisted accidentally when only metadata/reference should be stored;
- persistence/native UI tests.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(data): add recent and pinned data activity`

