## Goal
Expose the existing PostgreSQL user/role backend through a safe native security workbench instead of rewriting the backend.

## Scope
- Users/Roles activity or Explorer Security section;
- list/detail roles;
- create/alter/drop role;
- membership grant/revoke;
- database/schema/table/sequence privileges where supported;
- privilege matrix view;
- password change flow with secret-safe handling;
- DDL/source preview where useful;
- provider capability gating for SQLite.

## Acceptance
- reuse existing `user_service`/`PostgresUserManager` where applicable;
- identifiers/privileges use existing allowlist/quoting safety;
- no secret shown in logs/audit text;
- destructive role drop and privilege changes are confirmation-aware;
- live PG service/UI tests;
- unsupported grant classes remain explicit rather than implied.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(security): add native users roles and privilege workbench`

Parent Goal: #182
Depends on: #196
Authority: `docs/goals/goal-phase-d-monitoring.md`

## Goal
Expand Monitoring into a useful administration surface for contention, storage and maintenance.

## Scope
PostgreSQL:
- locks + blocked/blocker relationships;
- transactions and age;
- database/table/index size;
- table scan/index usage stats;
- server/version summary;
- VACUUM / ANALYZE / VACUUM ANALYZE actions;
- explicit admin/long-running confirmations.

SQLite:
- expose only meaningful file/database stats and maintenance operations supported safely.

## Acceptance
- blocked/blocker view resolves exact sessions;
- size values are correctly formatted without precision loss;
- maintenance actions are capability-gated and confirmation-aware;
- no maintenance SQL is constructed in UI;
- refresh/poll cost bounded;
- live PG tests + provider/service/native UI coverage.

Merge independently after D01.
Suggested commit: `feat(monitoring): add locks statistics and maintenance`

Parent Goal: #182
Authority: `docs/goals/goal-phase-d-monitoring.md`

## Goal
Replace the Monitoring placeholder with a real provider-aware monitoring service and native activity.

## Scope
PostgreSQL first:
- sessions/process list;
- active queries;
- duration/state/wait metadata;
- cancel query;
- terminate session with stronger confirmation;
- refresh/poll lifecycle with bounded frequency;
- open query text in SQL editor;
- capability model and provider adapter.

SQLite:
- expose only meaningful supported state; do not fake server sessions.

## Architecture
Add `MonitoringService` + provider port/adapters. UI must not query `pg_stat_activity` directly.

## Acceptance
- native Monitoring activity replaces COMING SOON placeholder;
- PG session/query list works on live fixture;
- cancel/terminate target exact backend identity and cannot affect unrelated execution;
- destructive/admin confirmation is explicit;
- polling stops when view inactive/app closes;
- structured errors + service/provider/UI tests.

Merge independently to latest main.
Suggested commit: `feat(monitoring): add sessions and active query workbench`

